<article>
  <h3>The Importance of Typography in Web Design</h3>
  <p>
    Typography is one of the most critical aspects of web design. It affects not only the aesthetic
    appeal of your website but also its usability and accessibility. Good typography enhances
    readability, establishes hierarchy, and creates a pleasant reading experience.
  </p>

  <h4>Key Principles</h4>
  <p>When implementing typography systems, consider these fundamental principles:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Maintain consistent line heights for comfortable reading</li>
    <li>Use fluid scaling to adapt to different viewport sizes</li>
    <li>Establish clear visual hierarchy through size and weight</li>
    <li>Ensure sufficient contrast between text and background</li>
    <li>Optimize line length for readability (45-75 characters)</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Responsive Typography</h4>
  <p>
    Modern web design demands responsive typography that adapts seamlessly to various screen sizes.
    Traditional media query breakpoints create abrupt size changes, while fluid typography using CSS
    <code>clamp()</code> provides smooth scaling across all viewport widths.
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    Good typography makes the reading experience effortless and enjoyable, allowing content to speak
    for itself without distraction.
  </blockquote>

  <h5>Implementation Details</h5>
  <p>The typography system on this page uses the following approach:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Base font size scales from 16px to 18px using clamp()</li>
    <li>Headings scale proportionally with viewport width</li>
    <li>Line heights are optimized for each text element</li>
    <li>Font families are assigned semantic roles (title, body, quote)</li>
  </ol>

  <h6>Testing Different Viewports</h6>
  <p>
    Resize your browser window to see how the typography scales smoothly without any abrupt jumps.
    The fluid system ensures optimal readability at every size, from mobile devices at 320px width
    to large desktop displays at 1920px and beyond.
  </p>
</article>
